# X-Ray.Content — this fork's own ignore rules. Upstream Xberg's rules live in
# .reference/.gitignore, where their tree-root-anchored paths still resolve, and where an
# upstream patch touching .gitignore lands. Do not merge the two files.

# ── .NET build output ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Anchored to /dotnet/ on purpose. A bare `**/bin/` would also exclude directories inside
# .reference/, and git will not descend into an excluded directory, so upstream's own
# negations (e.g. !packages/dart/bin/download_libs.dart) could not re-include anything there.
/dotnet/**/bin/
/dotnet/**/obj/
*.nupkg
*.snupkg
/artifacts/

# ── IDE / editor ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.user
*.suo
*.userprefs
*.DotSettings.user

# ── Rust dev helpers under dotnet/tools/ ──────────────────────────────────────
/dotnet/tools/*/target/

# ── Golden reference sets for the C# port ─────────────────────────────────────
# Generated locally by `dotnet/tools/xberg-reference-gen`, one directory per xberg feature
# configuration (`--out`), and regenerated rather than committed — they are large,
# machine-specific in places (pdf_oxide's font cache), and tied to whatever the Rust tree
# in .reference/ is at.
/test_documents-goldens-*/

# ── OS noise ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*~

# ── Local environment ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.local
